<title>PORTUGAL: Heavy trade in Portugal's BCP a portfolio switch.</title>
<headline>Heavy trade in Portugal's BCP a portfolio switch.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A single trade on Thursday totalling some one percent of the share capital of Portugal's largest quoted bank, Banco Comercial Portugues, was a portfolio switch by non-resident institutions, a bank spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;It was an adjustment of portfolios by non-resident institutional investors,&quot; the spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Banco Comercial was gaining 20 escudos at 3,490 in exceptional turnover of 2.13 million shares. But the portfolio switch had involved a single block of 1.5 million shares also at 3,490, the spokesman said. ($1=188 escudos)</p>
</text>
